Arara Code: let extension views choose their position in the Source Control container.

Why a patch: extension views contributed to `scm` get no order and always land below
Graph. The container gains a viewOrderDelegate that reads `"group": "position@N"`
(Changes = 1, Graph = 2) so an extension view can sit between them. No product
logic, view ids or texts live in this public patch.
Touches: src/vs/workbench/contrib/scm/browser/scm.contribution.ts

--- a/src/vs/workbench/contrib/scm/browser/scm.contribution.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/contrib/scm/browser/scm.contribution.ts
@@ -62,6 +62,13 @@
 	alwaysUseContainerInfo: true,
 	order: 2,
 	hideIfEmpty: true,
+	// Arara: extension views can pick their slot with `"group": "position@N"` (Changes = 1, Graph = 2)
+	viewOrderDelegate: {
+		getOrder: (group?: string) => {
+			const match = group ? /^position@(\d+(?:\.\d+)?)$/.exec(group) : null;
+			return match ? Number(match[1]) : undefined;
+		}
+	},
 }, ViewContainerLocation.Sidebar, { doNotRegisterOpenCommand: true });
 
 const viewsRegistry = Registry.as<IViewsRegistry>(ViewContainerExtensions.ViewsRegistry);
